From e266efe423be5da4047b2ed775c1831e73f74c81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:25:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make Notifications a real tab: role access, unread badge,
 feeds and event deep links
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The panel already had a Notifications page but the tab was easy to lose: it was
labelled "Push Notifications", it was hidden for the super admin whenever their
stored `accessTab` predated it, and nothing told an admin when an event arrived.

* **Role access.** The tab's key (`notifications`) is the role-access checkbox
  in `utils/TabArray.js` and is now labelled "Notifications". It rides along
  with role management (`user`) exactly like Plans & Trials, so the super admin
  can open the inbox without first granting themselves the new key. A role that
  has neither sees an explicit "No access to notifications" card instead of the
  list.
* **Unread badge.** The sidebar (and the phone "More" drawer) shows the unread
  event count, polled every 60 s and cleared the moment the tab is opened.
* **Two feeds, one list.** All / Events / Sent by admin chips, filtered on the
  server (`feed`) rather than in the browser, so pagination stays honest.
* **Events lead somewhere.** An event row opens the tab it is about — order and
  delivery actions → Shop Orders, registration → Salons, renewal → Plans,
  booking request → Booking Requests.
* **Mark all read** next to the chips, and the page zeroes the badge on open.
